course: dictionary
lesson: 11863
title: A Scottish word: bonny
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Bonny is a word from Scotland and northern England. It usually means pretty or attractive. Check the words around it: «The bonny village sat beside the loch, with white cottages and flowers in every window.» Cottages and flowers are pretty things, so bonny means pretty here.
explain: Bonny can also describe a baby. «The bonny baby had rosy cheeks and chubby arms.» Rosy cheeks and chubby arms are signs of a healthy baby, so bonny here means healthy-looking and plump. Always swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: You will meet bonny in songs, such as «My Bonnie Lies over the Ocean», and in everyday talk, such as «a bonny wee lass». Writers use bonny to give a story a Scottish feeling.
fact: Bonny is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like a bonny baby or a bonny village.
fact: «Bonny» means pretty or attractive.
fact: «Bonny» can also mean healthy-looking, especially a plump, healthy baby.
fact: Bonny is a word from Scotland and northern England.
fact: Writers use bonny to give a story a Scottish feeling.
exercise: «The bonny village sat beside the loch.» What does bonny mean here? | Dark and empty | Very loud | *Pretty or attractive | Cold and windy
exercise: «The bonny baby had rosy cheeks and chubby arms.» What does bonny suggest about the baby? | Very tired and thin | Angry and loud | *Healthy-looking and plump | Lost in the crowd
exercise: Bonny is a word from which places? | The Sahara Desert | *Scotland and northern England | Antarctica | The middle of the sea
test: «The bonny lass at the fair won first prize.» Which meaning fits best? | Sleepy and cross | *Pretty or attractive | Very tall | Quiet and shy
test: Ella says bonny is a Scottish word and she does not know it. What is the best way to work out its meaning? | *Read the words around it, then swap in a meaning to check | Guess that it means loud | Change it into a noun | Skip it and never read that sentence again
exam: What does bonny mean in «The bonny baby slept soundly, her cheeks pink and round»? | Angry and loud | Lost in the dark | *Healthy-looking and plump | Very old
